 "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The World of Entertainment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Famous Friend", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "  You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress.  <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">A big agent <span class=\"strong\">is championing</span> him.</span> <br/><br/> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect </span> to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Groomers <span class=\"strong\">have lightened</span> his hair.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an  action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it.  Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in writing.  <br/><br/> Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"am/are/is +  being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Now he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is being championed </span> by a big agent.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">His hair <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has been lightened</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "His hair has been lightened.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He is being dressed by the trendiest designers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He is being touted as the next big thing! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He has been transformed into the star Beverly always thought he would be.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He has been groomed.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Habits in the Past: Used to and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> to talk about past habits which are now finished.  There is an idea that circumstances have changed.  You do not use it to talk about what happened at a past time. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Both <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> talk about past habits which no longer exist, but there are a couple of things to note about the usage of these expressions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  <ol><li><span class=\"strong\">Would</span>  cannot be used to talk about past states.  You must use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>.<br/> For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I used to have a dog.<br/> <s>I would have a dog.</s> </span></li>  <li>You use used to to talk about regular, important habitual behavior.  <br/> For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I used to smoke.<br/>  <s>I would smoke.</s></span></li></ol><br/>  Look at the chart for the rules about structuring sentences with <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>.  Notice the change in spelling of <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Positive Statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> know you when you were plain old Trev.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative Statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">didn't use to</span>  know you when you were plain old Trev.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Did I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">use to</span> know you when you were plain old Trev? </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "She used to worry that he would forget her when he started rising. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He used to tell her that was impossible. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He would always say \u201cYou are never being replaced as my personal confidant!\u201d", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Beverly would think about that every time she looked at the picture of them on her dresser. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "\u201cI used to know you when you were plain old Trev,\u201d she'd think.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "scrapbook", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bbook with \u200bempty \u200bpages where you can \u200bstick \u200bnewspaper \u200barticles, \u200bpictures, etc. that you have \u200bcollected and \u200bwant to \u200bkeep", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's collected a scrapbook of clippings and photos of his rise to stardom.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about someone famous.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "clipping", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an \u200barticle \u200bcut from a \u200bnewspaper", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Beverly collected a scrapbook of clippings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "plain old", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not at all unusual, interesting, or special", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I used to know you when you were plain old Trev.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to champion", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to fight for or speak in support of a group of people or a belief", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now he is being championed by a big agent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to groom", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bprepare someone for a \u200bspecial \u200bjob or \u200bactivity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  He has been groomed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cryptically", "type": "name"}, {"content": "mysterious and \u200bdifficult to \u200bunderstand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This year, Beverly got a note that cryptically read, \u2018when I'm in town'.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to transfigure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bchange the \u200bappearance of a \u200bperson or thing very much, usually in a very \u200bpositive and often \u200bspiritual way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is being transfigured!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unwavering", "type": "name"}, {"content": "never \u200bchanging or \u200bbecoming \u200bweaker", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You used to think I'd forget your constant unwavering support.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a 200 word dialogue between two friends talking about how they used to follow the same music or film celebrity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about what you used to do, what information you would look for, pictures you used to have on your wall, and other things you would collect or watch.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Enhance your dialogue with vocabulary for music or film.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice your dialogue aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read it with another student, first taking one role, then the other.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a dialogue between two friends talking about how they used to follow the same music or film celebrity", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use vocabulary for music or film to enhance the dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my dialogue aloud with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}